Diagnostic-only persistence for the existing Normal-WB ramoops console.

Default off and additionally gated by ramoops.console_flush_diag=1. Reuse the
reviewed target logger in the source kernel so that a failed SCM return and
intentional reset can be distinguished. No PMSG/dmesg, device permissions,
watchdogs, secure ownership or handoff instructions are changed.

--- a/kernel/Kconfig.kexec
+++ b/kernel/Kconfig.kexec
@@ -183,4 +183,19 @@
 	  the computation behind the value provided through the
 	  /sys/kernel/crash_elfcorehdr_size attribute.
 
+config KEXEC_RAMOOPS_FLUSH_DIAG
+	bool "Diagnostic PoC flush after native ramoops console writes"
+	depends on ARM64 && PSTORE_CONSOLE && PSTORE_RAM=y
+	default n
+	help
+	  Build a temporary kexec diagnostic option for a Normal-WB ramoops
+	  console. It remains disabled unless ramoops.console_flush_diag=1 is
+	  explicitly supplied on the kernel command line. After each console
+	  write, clean its complete validated RAM zone to the point of coherency
+	  and complete a system DSB. PMSG and dmesg writes are unaffected.
+
+	  Cleaning the complete zone after every console write can substantially
+	  slow boot and change timing. This is for a bounded diagnostic test,
+	  not a general-purpose ramoops persistence or kexec fix.
+
 endmenu
